>>>>      FIFO reset =E2=80=93 CTRL[1] bits
>>>> 4. Program the CARD_RESET register with a value of 0 for the bit
>>>> corresponding to the card number; This can be done at any time whe=
n
>>>> the card is connected to the controller. This programming asserts =
the
>>>> RST_n signal and resets the card.
>>>> 5. Wait for minimum of 1 =CE=BCs or cclk_in period, which ever is =
greater
>>>> 6. After a minimum of 1 =CE=BCs, the application should program a =
value of
>>>> 0 into the CARD_RESET register for the bit corresponding to the ca=
rd
>>>> number. This de-asserts the RST_n signal and takes the card out of=
 reset.
>>>> 7. The application can program a new CMD only after a minimum of 2=
00 us
